
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Line chart native tests
-----------------------
line_chart_widget/test_main.cpp tests the production widget against a recording
display, without hardware or networking. It covers point mapping, all four
clipping edges, gaps, uneven sample spacing, timestamps, markers, empty/single
readings, 100 samples, and invalid-input logging without partial drawing.
Y-scale tests cover signed and fractional labels, custom intervals, label
gutters, text bounds, tick counts, text-state reset, and invalid/dense scales.
Bar-chart checks cover zero baselines, proportional widths/heights, clipping,
tiny positive amounts, dry/missing dates, 3-pixel zero markers and bar gaps,
fractional-inch labels, and
invalid-input logging without partial drawing.

From the repository root, using an installed C++11 compiler (PowerShell):

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest\line_chart_widget\stubs -Isrc\widgets src\widgets\line_chart_widget.cpp test\line_chart_widget\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-line-chart-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-line-chart-tests.exe" }

Clang++ or "zig c++" can be used in place of g++. The stubs are exclusively for
this native test command; the normal PlatformIO firmware build uses the actual
Arduino and display headers.

Numeric history native tests
----------------------------
These tests use the same ArduinoJson dependency as the firmware. Build from the
repository root after the normal PlatformIO build has restored dependencies.
Use g++, clang++, or "zig c++":

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc\adafruitio "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" src\adafruitio\numeric_history.cpp test\numeric_history\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-history-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-history-tests.exe" }

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest\numeric_history\stubs -Isrc\adafruitio "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" src\adafruitio\adafruitio_manager.cpp src\adafruitio\feed_catalog.cpp src\adafruitio\numeric_history.cpp test\numeric_history\test_manager.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-history-manager-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-history-manager-tests.exe" }

The first suite covers strict UTC/fractional timestamp parsing, hourly and
custom buckets, partial windows, gaps, duplicate IDs versus repeated values,
raw extrema, circular bearings/cancellation, malformed responses, pagination
header formats, and 1,500 samples across 15 pages. The second compiles the real
manager against fake HTTP/TLS/FreeRTOS interfaces (no device or credentials)
to exercise complete-only publication, query/cursor construction, shared
request accounting, retry timing, stale-result retention, successful empty
windows, mid-page failure, cancellation during HTTP, throttling, cursor loops,
and the unchanged latest-value/alert-history response paths.
Daily-history checks cover 14 completed UTC dates, midnight boundaries, local
DST independence, the export's 141-record daily-max fixture, conflicting totals,
154 records across pages, and alignment-mode changes/validation.
Local-calendar endpoint checks cover UTC advancing before local midnight,
advancement after local midnight, and standard time after the DST transition.

Weather descriptor compile-time tests
-------------------------------------
weather_descriptor/test_main.cpp checks all six weather words, rule precedence,
strict threshold boundaries, and invalid pressure inputs using static_assert.
Successful compilation runs all checks; no hardware or executable is needed.
From the repository root (PowerShell), using PlatformIO's installed compiler:

& "$env:USERPROFILE\.platformio\packages\toolchain-xtensa-esp32\bin\xtensa-esp32-elf-g++.exe" -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc -c test\weather_descriptor\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-weather-descriptor-tests.o"

Wind direction statistics native tests
--------------------------------------
wind_direction_stats/test_main.cpp covers 16-point compass sectors and edges,
wrap-around through north, speed weighting, steadiness, calm/invalid samples,
cancelling winds, and the smallest covering range. From the repository root:

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc src\screens\wind_direction_stats.cpp test\wind_direction_stats\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-wind-direction-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-wind-direction-tests.exe" }
